# {{ .prefix }}-executing-direct

The direct implementation chain node for work whose clear outcome, solution shape, boundary, and verification{{if ne .profile "core"}} warrant neither an ADR nor a plan{{else}} are already approved and direct{{end}}.

## When to invoke

Load this skill before directly mutating files when the outcome, solution shape, boundary, and verification are clear, and no independent need for brainstorming{{if ne .profile "core"}}, an ADR, or a plan{{end}} fires. If a material choice or clarification is needed, invoke brainstorming;{{if ne .profile "core"}} if an ADR or plan is warranted, use that workflow instead.{{end}}

<!-- awf:include production-code-outline-approval -->

## Procedure

1. Before mutation, evaluate continuity independently. This skill may run without an effort. If continuity materially helps, invoke `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}`; if an effort already exists, validate its fixed identity and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`, preserve one writer, and use its managed worktree when present. Otherwise omit effort and memory fields. {{if eq .profile "core"}}Project documentation, source, tests, and repository history remain authoritative{{else}}Repository sources and current-state documentation remain authoritative{{end}}. Re-read any settled design brief and, per `{{ .layout.maintainableCodeDesign }}`, assess bounded enabling refactoring before editing and preserve settled boundaries.
2. Implement only the agreed change. Add or update focused tests, and keep documentation current in the same change.
3. Run the project's required formatting and verification commands. Fix the cause of every failure; do not weaken expected behavior.
4. Complete one coherent transaction with verification and a commit, following the project's commit discipline, unless the caller explicitly requires a larger approved change set in one commit or forbids commits.
5. For an effort-backed outcome, after each independently resumable committed and reviewed change run the routine checkpoint below before continuing.

<!-- awf:include checkpoint-routine -->

6. Evaluate review independently. Invoke `{{ .prefix }}-reviewing-impl` for meaningful breadth, non-obvious logic, contract or compatibility effects, migrations, security, concurrency, data-loss risk, substantive verification judgment, or uncertainty. Skip only locally obvious, low-risk, directly verified work where independent review is unlikely to find meaningful hidden consequences. Effort-backed work returns to `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` after assurance settles or is explicitly skipped.{{if ne .profile "core"}} For effort-free work, the parent owns any applicable deferred ADR/plan terminal artifact transaction after assurance settles or is explicitly skipped, using `{{ .prefix }}-adr-lifecycle`, the gate, and audit obligations; otherwise it concludes after verification.{{else}} For effort-free work, it concludes after verification.{{end}}

## Boundaries

<!-- awf:include implementation-autonomy -->
- Re-evaluate brainstorming if implementation exposes a material choice or clarification, and return there when it fires rather than silently expanding scope or accepting a workaround.
{{if ne .profile "core"}}- Re-evaluate planning when sequencing, coordination, or resumability may materially help; write a plan only when that independent need fires.{{end}}
- Preserve unrelated work in the checkout.
